Third-party components
----------------------

The components below keep their own licenses. Each license text is kept next to
the component in this repository, or is part of the Rust crate's published source
(in Cargo's registry after `cargo fetch`, and on https://crates.io).

Rust crates compiled into the programs (versions as in Cargo.lock):

- Typst 0.15.1 (typst, typst-layout, typst-pdf, typst-html, typst-kit and the
  typst-* crates they use; linked by crates/gd-typst with its default `embedded`
  feature): Apache License 2.0. The fonts typst-assets embeds keep their own
  licenses, listed in that crate's NOTICE: Libertinus Serif (SIL Open Font License
  1.1), New Computer Modern (GUST Font License 1.0; NewCM10-Regular GPL-3.0-or-later
  with the font exception), DejaVu Sans Mono (Bitstream Vera license, DejaVu changes
  in the public domain), and the Foxit PDF standard fonts (PDFium's BSD-style
  license).
- OpenSSL 3 (openssl-src, built and linked statically on Linux only, for Typst's
  package downloader): Apache License 2.0. macOS and Windows use the system's TLS.
- tree-sitter 0.25 (crates/gd-pyscan, crates/gd-rustdoc), tree-sitter-python 0.25 and
  tree-sitter-rust 0.24: MIT License. `guidedog --licenses` prints these notices.
- serde_json 1 and serde 1 (crates/gd-json): MIT License or Apache License 2.0, at
  the user's option.
- ureq 2 (crates/gd-fetch, HTTP and HTTPS): MIT License or Apache License 2.0, at
  the user's option. Its TLS stack: rustls 0.23 (Apache License 2.0, ISC License or
  MIT License, at the user's option); rustls-webpki (ISC License); rustls-pki-types
  (MIT or Apache-2.0); ring 0.17 (ISC License, with code from BoringSSL under the
  Apache License 2.0 and the ISC License; see its LICENSE files); untrusted (ISC
  License); subtle (BSD-3-Clause); zeroize (Apache-2.0 or MIT); and webpki-roots,
  which embeds Mozilla's root certificates (Community Data License Agreement,
  Permissive, Version 2.0).
- The other crates these depend on are each under a permissive license: mostly MIT
  or Apache-2.0 (often both, at the user's option), and also BSD-2-Clause,
  BSD-3-Clause, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, BSL-1.0, 0BSD, CC0-1.0, Unlicense, and MPL-2.0
  (option-ext), CDLA-Permissive-2.0 (webpki-roots). `cargo metadata` lists every
